    <h2>1. What is a List in HTML?</h2>
    <p>A list is used to show items one by one. For example - a shopping list, a menu list, or steps to do something.</p>
    <p>There are <b>2 main types</b> of lists in HTML:</p>
    <div class="note"><b>1. Unordered List (ul)</b> = Bullet points ( • ) — Order does not matter<br><b>2. Ordered List (ol)</b> = Numbers ( 1, 2, 3 ) — Order matters</div>
    <p>Both lists use <b>&lt;li&gt;</b> tag for each item. <b>li = List Item</b></p>
    <h2>2. Unordered List - &lt;ul&gt;</h2>
    <p>Use this when the order does not matter. Example: Shopping List.</p>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="tag">&lt;ul&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;li&gt;</span><span class="text">Apple</span><span class="tag">&lt;/li&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;li&gt;</span><span class="text">Banana</span><span class="tag">&lt;/li&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;li&gt;</span><span class="text">Mango</span><span class="tag">&lt;/li&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;/ul&gt;</span>
    </code></div>
    <div class="result"><b>Result:</b><ul style="margin-left:20px;line-height:1.8"><li>Apple</li><li>Banana</li><li>Mango</li></ul></div>
    <h2>3. Ordered List - &lt;ol&gt;</h2>
    <p>Use this when the order matters. Example: Steps to make tea.</p>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="tag">&lt;ol&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;li&gt;</span><span class="text">Boil water</span><span class="tag">&lt;/li&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;li&gt;</span><span class="text">Add tea leaves</span><span class="tag">&lt;/li&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;li&gt;</span><span class="text">Add milk and sugar</span><span class="tag">&lt;/li&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;/ol&gt;</span>
    </code></div>
    <div class="result"><b>Result:</b><ol style="margin-left:20px;line-height:1.8"><li>Boil water</li><li>Add tea leaves</li><li>Add milk and sugar</li></ol></div>
    <h2>4. Change the Style - type Attribute</h2>
    <p>You can change bullets and numbers with the <b>type</b> attribute.</p>
    <table>
      <tr><th>List</th><th>type</th><th>Result</th></tr>
      <tr><td>Unordered</td><td>disc (default)</td><td>• Apple</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Unordered</td><td>circle</td><td>○ Apple</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Unordered</td><td>square</td><td>▪ Apple</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Ordered</td><td>1 (default)</td><td>1, 2, 3</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Ordered</td><td>A</td><td>A, B, C</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Ordered</td><td>a</td><td>a, b, c</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Ordered</td><td>I</td><td>I, II, III</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Ordered</td><td>i</td><td>i, ii, iii</td></tr>
    </table>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="tag">&lt;ul</span> <span class="attr">type</span>=<span class="val">"square"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><span class="text"> ... </span><span class="tag">&lt;/ul&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;ol</span> <span class="attr">type</span>=<span class="val">"A"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><span class="text"> ... </span><span class="tag">&lt;/ol&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;ol</span> <span class="attr">type</span>=<span class="val">"I"</span> <span class="attr">start</span>=<span class="val">"3"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><span class="text"> ... </span><span class="tag">&lt;/ol&gt;</span>
    </code></div>
    <div class="result"><b>Example:</b><ol type="A" style="margin-left:20px;line-height:1.8"><li>HTML</li><li>CSS</li><li>JavaScript</li></ol><ol type="I" start="3" style="margin-left:20px;line-height:1.8;margin-top:8px"><li>Starts from III</li><li>Next is IV</li></ol></div>
    <div class="note"><b>start attribute:</b> It tells from which number the list should start. Example: <b>start="5"</b> means list will start from 5.</div>
    <h2>5. Nested List - List Inside a List</h2>
    <p>When you put a list inside another list, it is called a <b>Nested List</b>. It is used for menus and sub-menus.</p>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="tag">&lt;ul&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;li&gt;</span><span class="text">Fruits</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;ul&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;li&gt;</span><span class="text">Apple</span><span class="tag">&lt;/li&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;li&gt;</span><span class="text">Mango</span><span class="tag">&lt;/li&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;/ul&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;/li&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;li&gt;</span><span class="text">Vegetables</span><span class="tag">&lt;/li&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;/ul&gt;</span>
    </code></div>
    <div class="result"><b>Result:</b><ul style="margin-left:20px;line-height:1.8"><li>Fruits<ul style="margin-left:20px"><li>Apple</li><li>Mango</li></ul></li><li>Vegetables</li></ul></div>
    <h2>6. Full Example - My Daily Routine</h2>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="tag">&lt;h2&gt;</span><span class="text">My Daily Routine</span><span class="tag">&lt;/h2&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;ol&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;li&gt;</span><span class="text">Wake up at 6 AM</span><span class="tag">&lt;/li&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;li&gt;</span><span class="text">Learn HTML</span><span class="tag">&lt;/li&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;li&gt;</span><span class="text">Practice Code</span><span class="tag">&lt;/li&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;/ol&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;h2&gt;</span><span class="text">Shopping List</span><span class="tag">&lt;/h2&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;ul&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;li&gt;</span><span class="text">Milk</span><span class="tag">&lt;/li&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;li&gt;</span><span class="text">Bread</span><span class="tag">&lt;/li&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;/ul&gt;</span>
    </code></div>
    <h2>7. Homework - Practice for 2 Minutes</h2>
    <p>Create a page with:</p>
    <p>1. An <b>Ordered List</b> of your 3 favourite subjects<br>2. An <b>Unordered List</b> of your 3 favourite foods<br>3. One <b>Nested List</b> - Fruits &gt; Apple, Mango</p>
    <div class="box"><b>Remember:</b> ul = Bullet List | ol = Number List | li = List Item | type = Change style | start = Start from any number</div>
    <p><b>Next Step:</b> After this lesson, go to <a href="/lesson6">Lesson 6 - Tables in HTML</a> to learn how to create tables.</p>
